spec:
  grid: 3x3 input, 9x9 output
  colors: exactly {black(0), blue(1), red(2)}
  pixel_counts:
    blue: exactly 3 [observed]
    red: 1-4 (placement mask)
    black: 2-5 (empty space)
  constraints:
    - at least 1 red pixel and at least 1 black pixel required
    - all 9 cells assigned to exactly one of {black, blue, red}
  transform: |
    output is h*h x w*w (=9x9). For each red pixel at (r,c),
    stamp full input grid into output block [r*h:(r+1)*h, c*w:(c+1)*w].
    All other blocks stay black.
